{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Legal Considerations When Negotiating Technology Contracts Agreements"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about service level agreements."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.   Define strategies to make terms of reference and supplier assessment processes, in technology acquisition, based on established protocols."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Writes simple texts on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, technological negotiation, and requirements on negotiation processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed to in Negative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When we want to express that something is not expected or required from someone or something, we can use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to in negative statements.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "However, you are not supposed to have access to this code unless the vendor fails to provide the promised services."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is, however, not always easy to find an IT contract. SLAs are not supposed to be offered upfront by the vendor."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Be supposed to in negative statements</span> is used to say that something is not expected or required to happen. </br></br>   Structure: </br></br>   <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">am/is/are</span> + <span class=\"strong\">not</span> +<span class=\"strong\">supposed to</span> + verb base form + complement </div> </br></br>  Take a look at the following examples: </br></br> <li>Legal considerations <span class=\"strong\">are not supposed to</span> be ignored by both parties in a negotiation. </li></br>  <li>A software vendor <span class=\"strong\">is not supposed to </span>make Service Level Agreements explicit. </li> "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Breaking down Service Level Agreements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A service level agreement states what the customer receives from the provider. It will not, however, define how the service will be provided. For a better understanding, check out the following features:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">A description of the service that the costumer procures: </span></br> Configuration protocols, domain name servers, and maintenance conditions</br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Reliability </span></br> A promise of the service availability and the scheduled outages limit</br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Responsiveness</span></br> The promptness and punctually of services and response to requests</br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Procedure for reporting problems</span></br> Specifications on what to do if a problem arises, how and who should be reported and the steps to follow to resolve a problem with efficiency </br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Consequences for not delivering the promised services</span></br> Reimbursement, or enabling the licensee to terminate the contract relationship"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "draft "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to write something before it is in its definitive form"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Drafting a technology contract (or dealing with the vendor's form) is an effort to ensure that your needs and expected contractual rights are laid out in the contract."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lay out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to explain something in a written way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Drafting a technology contract (or dealing with the vendor's form) is an effort to ensure that your needs and expected contractual rights are laid out in the contract."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "readily"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Escrow as insurance: if the product you purchased is essential and it cannot be replaced readily and supposedly the vendor goes out of business."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "supposedly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "related to what is commonly believed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Escrow as insurance: if the product you purchased is essential and it cannot be replaced readily and supposedly the vendor goes out of business."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comprehensible "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "easy to be understood"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is sometimes necessary to ask for them, and when 