ontent": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1, "id": 12}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le01ob06re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob06re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "IT negotiations demand from both parties, the customer and the software vendor, to have some legal considerations in mind. Whether it is just procuring a new software version, or putting into practice an expensive management system solution, drafting a technology contract (or dealing with the vendor's form) is an effort to ensure that your needs and expected contractual rights are laid out in the contract. Here, some of the legal considerations you should take into account will be discussed:"}, {"time": "29800", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Escrow as insurance: if the product you purchased is essential and it cannot be replaced readily and supposedly the vendor goes out of business, or the product you purchased is no longer made, you ought to have an escrow agreement so that you can have access to the source code as an insurance. However, you are not supposed to have access to this code unless the vendor fails to provide the promised services.\nService Level Agreements: An SLA should describe what cloud services are promised to the customer. This is, however, not always easy to find an IT contract. SLAs are not supposed to be offered upfront by the vendor, so it is sometimes necessary to ask for them, and when you do get them, they are not fully comprehensible. SLAs ought to be a guarantee for the cloud users to access the procured services or get customer support with a pre-established schedule. An SLA can include an insurance in the case that the vendor doesn't meet its obligations."}, {"time": "91000", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob06re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "To summarize, vendors are not supposed to make these legal considerations explicit. Nevertheless, an IT legal consultant ought to ask for them because they can provide indemnification for the customer in case there are liabilities in the services provided by the vendor."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le01ob06re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n7le01ob06re5vsc01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": ""}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}